      impact: Programs in a workspace can't use your SSH keys for servers other than Git hosts.
              Git over SSH still works.
      remedy: Start your SSH agent before Puddle, so SSH_AUTH_SOCK is set.
      note:   SSH to servers other than Git hosts gets no key from Puddle. Start your agent
              (ssh-agent, gpg-agent, 1Password or Bitwarden) in the session that starts Puddle so
              that SSH_AUTH_SOCK is set, or name its socket in the settings (`ui.ssh_agent_pipe`).
              Git hosts need no agent: Puddle ends their SSH sessions itself, so Git over SSH is
              not affected.
